  "prefLabel": "Ban 103.05 Legal Division",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ban 103.05 Legal Division. The legal division, headed by the general counsel, shall:\n\n(a) Investigate, mediate, and resolve consumer complaints against institutions under the supervision of the commissioner;\n\n(b) Provide legal support for administrative actions taken by the department, and prosecute and take enforcement actions against institutions under the supervision of the commissioner;\n\n(c) Provide legal counsel to the department;\n\n(d) Assist the commissioner in rulemaking and legislation;\n\n(e) Provide information and assistance to members of the public relating to matters under the department’s regulatory authority; and\n\n(f) Administer and coordinate the department’s responses to requests for governmental records.\n\nSource. #10258, eff 1-24-13; ss by #14096, eff 10-3-24 (formerly Ban 103.04)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ban100.html"
